that parent's `dependencyManagement` section." That's the standard Spring Boot way of handling this.

However, that's where the confusion started to creep in. I know that `spring-boot-starter-parent` version `4.0.6` itself has specific dependencies it relies on, like `spring-expression`, 
`spring-webmvc`, `micrometer-core`, and `tomcat-embed-core`. Now, in the *root* `pom.xml`, I had explicitly tried to override some of these individual dependencies within its 
