Summary: Remove incorrectly placed jackson-bom.version tag from root pom.xml

Reasoning:
It seems I've made a mistake in my previous attempt to resolve the build issue. I'm truly sorry about that; the fix I implemented clearly didn't achieve the desired outcome. The error 
message, "Unrecognised tag: 'jackson-bom.version'", directly points to the problem. My initial thought was to simply declare `<jackson-bom.version>3.2.3</jackson-bom.version>` within the 
`<properties>` section of our `pom.xml`.

However, I'm now realizing the nuance here. The `jackson-bom.version` property isn't directly defined in our root `pom.xml`. Instead, it originates from the `spring-boot-starter-parent`'s
`pom.xml`. The standard approach to overriding a property defined in a parent POM is indeed to declare it in our child's `<properties>` section. I thought I had done this correctly, but 
Maven's persistent complaint about an "unrecognized tag" suggests a more fundamental structural issue within the XML itself, rather than just a value problem.

Upon reviewing the output from the `file_editor` in my previous execution, I've spotted the exact cause of the invalid XML structure. I see this snippet:

