To confirm this, I ran `mvn dependency:tree -pl task-service`. The output from that command confirmed my suspicion: `+- org.apache.commons:commons-text:jar:1.9:compile`. This definitively
tells me that `commons-text:1.9` is a direct, explicit dependency of `task-service`.

My plan is straightforward now: I need to edit the `task-service/pom.xml` file. The goal is to remove the explicit declaration of `commons-text` from there. By doing so, I'll ensure that 
`task-service` no longer tries to dictate its own version of `commons-text` and will instead inherit the version defined in the parent `pom.xml`'s `dependencyManagement`, which is 
`1.10.0`.

Before I make any changes, though, I need to actually *see* the current dependency declaration for `commons-text` within `task-service/pom.xml` to be absolutely sure what I'm dealing 
